            <ArticleTitle>Case records of the Massachusetts General Hospital: Case 34-2012: a 27-year-old woman in Ethiopia with severe pain, bleeding, and shock during labor.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1839-45</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1056/NEJMcpc1209508</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 27-year-old woman was admitted to a hospital in Ethiopia because of severe abdominal pain during labor, with cessation of contractions. She had been in labor at home, pushing for 24 hours. On arrival at the hospital 3 hours later, she was in shock. A procedure was performed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
